# Production: connect to the ObjectStack server.
# Defaults to same-origin (empty). The published @object-ui/console
# package is meant to be embedded in any ObjectStack server, so we
# MUST NOT bake in a specific origin here. Demo-only deployments
# (e.g. demo.objectstack.ai on Vercel) inject VITE_SERVER_URL at
# build time via their deploy environment.
VITE_SERVER_URL=
VITE_USE_MOCK_SERVER=false

# ── Sentry error tracking: OPT-IN AT BUILD TIME, never committed here ───────
#
# ⛔ DO NOT COMMIT A DSN IN THIS FILE. `apps/console/src/__tests__/
# env-production-telemetry-endpoint.test.ts` fails the build if you do, and
# the reason is not style:
#
# `@object-ui/console` publishes a PRE-BUILT SPA (`files: ["dist"]`,
# `prepublishOnly: pnpm build`). ONE artifact, built once from this file, is
# what every consumer embeds — the hosted SaaS console AND the on-premises /
# air-gapped EE images. Vite inlines every `VITE_*` here into that bundle as a
# frozen object literal, so a DSN committed here is a live third-party
# telemetry endpoint compiled into the artifact that lands inside customer
# networks. It cannot be removed or switched off afterwards: the
# `VITE_SENTRY_ENABLED` kill switch is read off that same frozen literal, so
# on a shipped bundle it is `undefined` forever and editing env vars or this
# file on the deployed host changes nothing.
#
# That is exactly what happened: an air-gapped EE deployment was measured
# sending 14 Sentry envelopes per session to sentry.io carrying IP and
# User-Agent PII, with no way for the customer to turn it off
# (objectstack-ai/cloud#1508, objectstack-ai/objectui#5522).
#
# The posture instead: absent DSN ⇒ `initSentry()` returns false and
# `@sentry/react` is never even imported (the vendor-sentry chunk is not
# fetched). Deployments that WANT error reporting — the hosted SaaS/demo build
# — inject the DSN in their own deploy environment at build time, the same way
# they already inject VITE_SERVER_URL:
#
#   VITE_SENTRY_DSN=https://<key>@<org>.ingest.sentry.io/<project>
#   VITE_SENTRY_SEND_DEFAULT_PII=true   # opt in to IP + User-Agent, off by default
#
# Other knobs, all optional and inert without a DSN:
# VITE_SENTRY_ENABLED=false          # force-off even when a DSN was injected
# VITE_SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT=production # defaults to Vite's MODE
# VITE_SENTRY_RELEASE=               # injected by CI as VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA when available
# VITE_SENTRY_TRACES_SAMPLE_RATE=0.1
# VITE_SENTRY_REPLAY=false
